   "start": 0.24,
   "text": "Peristalsis propels. Distention is again the stimulus. A contraction ring forms behind the chyme. Here, circular muscle contracts and longitudinal muscle relaxes. This is the propulsive segment. Just ahead, the pattern reverses. Longitudinal muscle contracts, circular muscle relaxes, and a receiving segment opens. The ring moves forward, pushing the chyme along."
